From 57fad81fd661354c4c7977f656e78beec65d29f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noel Blatter <noel.blatter@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 23:44:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Import of differometor: check JAX functions on their code
 objects, load the CSR kernels on first use

_tuning.apply() made sure that two JAX functions are the ones it expects by
reading their source text. inspect.getsource reads and tokenizes the whole
file each time: 2.6 ms for the two calls on an M4, a third of the import of
differometor. The same questions are now asked of the compiled functions (the
names they refer to, their string constants), which takes 20 microseconds and
gives the same answers for jax 0.9.0. All measures are still reported as "on".

scipy.sparse._sparsetools is only used by _CondensedLU. With the native kernel
a run never gets there, so the module is loaded when it is first asked for
(0.4 to 0.5 ms). Setting fast._sparsetools = None still switches it off.

Docker (arm64, one CPU, shipped bytecode), 2 x 25 fresh processes each:
import differometor 3.86 -> 2.68 ms. Benchmark outputs bit-identical.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
